invariant: INV-16
file: srv_auth.c
catches: quic_loop_host
reason: the server signs its CertificateVerify with its P-256 key under
  WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever its ch_cfg.cpu states. The signature still
  verifies. test/quic_loop_widemul.h runs the r2 identity, a P-256 key,
  and requires a server whose ch_cfg.cpu holds
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to call no file under its own names.

--- old
        return p256_sign(widemul_answer(cfg), id->priv, digest, sig, cap, sig_len);
--- new
        return p256_sign(WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED, id->priv, digest, sig, cap, sig_len);
